{"units": [{"id": "pema-word8", "translation": "both, to remain and to send these things are hard for me beyond device"}, {"id": "pema-word9", "translation": "and to send these women is a pain, and it is hard to manage"}, {"id": "pema-word10", "translation": "it has"}, {"id": "pema-word11", "translation": "to me"}, {"id": "pema-word12", "translation": "these women"}, {"id": "pema-word13", "translation": "them"}, {"id": "pema-word14", "translation": "to send them without anger is difficult for me"}, {"id": "pema-word15", "translation": "Do not be ignorant"}, {"id": "pema-word16", "translation": "When judgment is absent"}, {"id": "pema-word17", "translation": "Without justice"}, {"id": "pemaino-orth1", "translation": "to harm, to damage"}, {"id": "pemaino-def1", "translation": "to harm, to damage"}, {"id": "pemaino-def2", "translation": "to suffer harm"}, {"id": "pemaino-note1", "translation": "Passive"}, {"id": "pemaino-note2", "translation": "Πάπταινε δ᾽ [But look around]"}, {"id": "pemaino-quote1", "translation": "lest you yourself be harmed on the way"}, {"id": "pemaino-word1", "translation": "But look around"}, {"id": "pemone-orth1", "translation": "harm, damage, calamity"}, {"id": "pemone-def1", "translation": "harm, damage, calamity"}, {"id": "pemone-note1", "translation": "This word too, like πῆμα [harm], is very common among the tragedians."}, {"id": "pemone-note2", "translation": "Ταὐτά τοι [The same things, you know]"}, {"id": "pemone-note3", "translation": "Οἵαις ὑπ᾽ [By what kind of]"}, {"id": "pemone-note4", "translation": "Θέλοιμ᾽ ἂν ὡς [I would wish that]"}, {"id": "pemone-note5", "translation": "Ὅτῳ τῆς νῦν [To whom of the present]"}, {"id": "pemone-note6", "translation": "Μυρίαις δὲ [And with countless]"}, {"id": "pemone-note7", "translation": "Τί ποτε ταῖσδ᾽ ἐνέζευξας εὑρὼν ἁμαρτοῦσαν ἐν [Why ever did you yoke these women, having found her erring in]"}, {"id": "pemone-note8", "translation": "where the meter requires πημοσύναις [calamities], which Hermann restored."}, {"id": "pemone-note9", "translation": "Οὐδ᾽ ἔχω [Nor do I have]"}, {"id": "pemone-note10", "translation": "Ἐς τάσδε σαυτὸν [Yourself to these women]"}, {"id": "pemone-note11", "translation": "Τόλμησόν ποτε πρὸς τὰς παρούσας [Dare at some point against the present]"}, {"id": "pemone-note12", "translation": "Ὅμως δ᾽ ἀνάγκη [But nevertheless necessity]"}, {"id": "pemone-note13", "translation": "Δόμος [House]"}, {"id": "pemone-note14", "translation": "Πῶς γάρ τις [For how could anyone]"}, {"id": "pemone-note15", "translation": "thus Canterus for πημονήν [harm]"}, {"id": "pemone-note16", "translation": "Πημονῆς δ᾽ [And of harm]"}, {"id": "pemone-note17", "translation": "Πημονῆς [Of harm]"}, {"id": "pemone-note18", "translation": "Ἀμήχανον [Impossible]"}, {"id": "pemone-note19", "translation": "Ὅσπερ Ἰὼ [Just as Io]"}, {"id": "pemone-quote1", "translation": "wandering, one calamity after another settles upon her"}, {"id": "pemone-quote2", "translation": "I am bent by his calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-quote3", "translation": "to meet with the greatest calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-quote4", "translation": "I may be released from the present calamity"}, {"id": "pemone-quote5", "translation": "bent by calamities and miseries"}, {"id": "pemone-quote6", "translation": "with calamities?"}, {"id": "pemone-quote7", "translation": "to learn how I may escape calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-quote8", "translation": "you brought to harbor with calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-quote9", "translation": "rightly, to think with calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-quote10", "translation": "to bear calamities for mortals"}, {"id": "pemone-quote11", "translation": "full of calamities too much"}, {"id": "pemone-quote12", "translation": "would he fence off the nets of calamity?"}, {"id": "pemone-quote13", "translation": "there is enough indeed"}, {"id": "pemone-quote14", "translation": "remedies"}, {"id": "pemone-quote15", "translation": "food of calamity"}, {"id": "pemone-quote16", "translation": "he released from calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-word1", "translation": "harm"}, {"id": "pemone-word2", "translation": "The same things, you know"}, {"id": "pemone-word3", "translation": "By what kind of"}, {"id": "pemone-word4", "translation": "I would wish that"}, {"id": "pemone-word5", "translation": "To whom of the present"}, {"id": "pemone-word6", "translation": "And with countless"}, {"id": "pemone-word7", "translation": "Why ever did you yoke these women, having found her erring in"}, {"id": "pemone-word8", "translation": "calamities"}, {"id": "pemone-word9", "translation": "Nor do I have"}, {"id": "pemone-word10", "translation": "Yourself to these women"}, {"id": "pemone-word11", "translation": "Dare at some point against the present"}, {"id": "pemone-word12", "translation": "But nevertheless necessity"}, {"id": "pemone-word13", "translation": "House"}, {"id": "pemone-word14", "translation": "For how could anyone"}, {"id": "pemone-word15", "translation": "harm"}, {"id": "pemone-word16", "translation": "And of harm"}, {"id": "pemone-word17", "translation": "Of harm"}, {"id": "pemone-word18", "translation": "Impossible"}, {"id": "pemone-word19", "translation": "Just as Io"}, {"id": "pemosyne-orth1", "translation": "calamity, harm"}, {"id": "pemosyne-def1", "translation": "the same as πημονή [calamity]"}, {"id": "pemosyne-note1", "translation": "Ibid."}, {"id": "pemosyne-note2", "translation": "for πημοναῖσιν [calamities] Hermann restored"}, {"id": "pemosyne-quote1", "translation": "You who share in the calamities of this man"}, {"id": "pemosyne-quote2", "translation": "calamities"}, {"id": "pemosyne-word1", "translation": "calamity"}, {"id": "pemosyne-word2", "translation": "calamities"}, {"id": "penelope-orth1", "translation": "Penelope"}, {"id": "penelope-def1", "translation": "was the title of a play by Aeschylus, mentioned in the Catalogue of plays, of which one fragment (186) survives."}, {"id": "pesas-orth1", "translation": "having stumbled"}, {"id": "pesas-def1", "translation": "Ag. 1624 erroneously for πταίσας [having stumbled]. See πταίω [to stumble]."}, {"id": "pesas-word1", "translation": "having stumbled"}, {"id": "pesas-word2", "translation": "to stumble"}, {"id": "piaino-orth1", "translation": "to fatten"}, {"id": "piaino-def1", "translation": "to fatten"}, {"id": "piaino-def2", "translation": "Figuratively, to exalt, to gladden"}, {"id": "piaino-note1", "translation": "Ἔγωγε μὲν [I at least]"}, {"id": "piaino-note2", "translation": "Ἀλλ᾽ ἡ σ᾽ [But she you]"}, {"id": "piaino-note3", "translation": "Πιαίνου [Fatten yourself]"}, {"id": "piaino-quote1", "translation": "I will fatten this land, a prophet hidden beneath enemy soil"}, {"id": "piaino-quote2", "translation": "some wingless rumor fattened"}, {"id": "piaino-quote3", "translation": "defiling justice"}, {"id": "piaino-word1", "translation": "I at least"}, {"id": "piaino-word2", "translation": "But she you"}, {"id": "piaino-word3", "translation": "Fatten yourself"}, {"id": "piasma-orth1", "translation": "nourishment"}, {"id": "piasma-def1", "translation": "nourishment"}, {"id": "piasma-note1", "translation": "with long iota"}, {"id": "piasma-note2", "translation": "Ἔνθα πεδίον Ἀσωπὸς ῥοαῖς ἄρδει [Where the Asopus waters the plain with its streams]"}, {"id": "piasma-note3", "translation": "Explained by the scholiast as λίπασμα [fat]. Not found elsewhere."}, {"id": "piasma-quote1", "translation": "a dear nourishment to the land of the Boeotians"}, {"id": "piasma-word1", "translation": "Where the Asopus waters the plain with its streams"}, {"id": "piasma-word2", "translation": "fat"}, {"id": "piezo-orth1", "translation": "to press"}, {"id": "piezo-def1", "translation": "to press"}, {"id": "piezo-note1", "translation": "Τοὺς δ᾽ [And them]"}, {"id": "piezo-note2", "translation": "Καὶ πρὸς [And against]"}, {"id": "piezo-note3", "translation": "Thus Abreschius for προσπιέζει [presses upon]."}, {"id": "piezo-quote1", "translation": "hunger presses the orphaned"}, {"id": "piezo-quote2", "translation": "lack of money presses"}, {"id": "piezo-word1", "translation": "And them"}, {"id": "piezo-word2", "translation": "And against"}, {"id": "piezo-word3", "translation": "presses upon"}, {"id": "pithanos-orth1", "translation": "persuasive"}, {"id": "pithanos-def1", "translation": "having the power of persuading, suited to persuading"}, {"id": "pithanos-note1", "translation": "Πιθανὸς ἄγαν [Exceedingly persuasive]"}, {"id": "pithanos-note2", "translation": "where others took it passively, as one who is easily persuaded, credulous, as Xenophon Cyrop. 2, 2, 10 called πιθανοὺς [persuadable] those who readily obey, i.e. compliant, πιθανοὶ δὲ οὕτως εἰσί πως ὥστε πρὼ εἰδέναι τὸ προσταττόμενον πρότερον πείθονται [and they are so persuadable that before knowing what is commanded they obey first], which Photius explained by εὐπειθεῖς [obedient]."}, {"id": "pithanos-quote1", "translation": "the female boundary is grazed"}, {"id": "pithanos-word1", "translation": "Exceedingly persuasive"}, {"id": "pithanos-word2", "translation": "persuadable"}, {"id": "pithanos-word3", "translation": "and they are so persuadable that before knowing what is commanded they obey first"}]}